# Cloudflare Pages header rules.
#
# Caching note, learned the hard way: this site's filenames never change, so an
# aggressive "immutable" cache is wrong here. It also gets applied to 404s,
# which means a browser that asks for a file before it exists can cache the
# failure and refuse to look again for as long as the rule says. Everything
# below therefore revalidates quickly. The cost is a tiny 304 request; the
# benefit is that an edit is visible immediately instead of days later.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/app.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
